# oracle: dihedral_style charmm with weight 0 next to pair_style lj/cut (the imd/bucky-plus-cnt example has
#   dihedral_coeff 1 3.100 2 180 0.0). Native DihedralCharmm::init_style checks the pair style and special_bonds
#   only "if (weightflag)" (src/MOLECULE/dihedral_charmm.cpp at b332f28; weightflag is set by a weight > 0), so
#   the dihedral runs with lj/cut. Measured with native LAMMPS (black box): with a weight 1.0 the same input stops
#   with "Dihedral charmm is incompatible with Pair style" (not in this case).
# oracle-inputs: w105cf_charmm_w0_lj.data
# oracle-compare: thermo=all rel=1e-12 abs=1e-14
units real
atom_style molecular
dimension 3
boundary f f f
read_data w105cf_charmm_w0_lj.data
pair_style lj/cut 10.0
bond_style harmonic
angle_style charmm
dihedral_style charmm
special_bonds lj/coul 0.0 0.0 0.0
pair_coeff 1 1 0.07 3.55
bond_coeff 1 305.0 1.4
angle_coeff 1 40.000 120.00 35.00 2.41620
dihedral_coeff 1 3.100 2 180 0.0
thermo_style custom step pe evdwl ebond eangle edihed
thermo_modify format float %.15g
run 0
